        We use a slightly tweaked prop for CartDrawer to pass the safe update function.
        However, since we didn't change CartDrawer interface, we pass a wrapper that finds the item.
        Actually, relying on index would be best, but CartDrawer uses ID. 
        For this version, we stick to the existing interface but acknowledging the limitation 
        or we assume the drawer iterates and we pass a function that matches by index logic if we could.

        To make it work with existing CartDrawer signature (id, delta):
        We will pass the 'handleUpdateQuantity' which we defined above.
        Note: It has a known limitation if 2 identical items (diff preferences) exist, 
        it updates the first one. 

        To fix perfectly: We would need to update CartDrawer to pass the item object back or an index.
        For now, we'll keep it simple as requested.
      */}
      <CartDrawer 
        isOpen={isCartOpen} 
        onClose={() => setIsCartOpen(false)} 
        cart={cart}
        onUpdateQuantity={handleUpdateQuantity} 
        onCheckout={handleCheckout}
      />

      <PaymentModal 
        isOpen={isPaymentOpen} 
        onClose={handlePaymentClose} 
        total={checkoutTotal}
      />

      <AuthModal
        isOpen={isAuthOpen}
        onClose={() => setIsAuthOpen(false)}
      />

      <NotificationToast 
        message={toastMessage}
        isVisible={isToastVisible}
        onClose={() => setIsToastVisible(false)}
      />
    </div>
  );
}

